## 4. How to answer when interviewers ask about real-time experience

This is where you need to be particularly careful.

Never claim that you worked on AWS or Kubernetes in production if you haven't.

But don't undersell your practical experience either.

If the interviewer asks:

"Do you have real-time experience with AWS and Kubernetes?"

You can answer:

Writing

I have around 10 years of experience in software development, primarily working with .NET technologies, REST APIs, and microservices.

Recently, I have expanded my technical skills into AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, and DevOps. I have completed hands-on practical implementations using these technologies, including building and deploying microservices-based applications inspired by real-world platforms like Netflix and JioMart.

I have worked on containerization, Kubernetes deployments, AWS services, and CI/CD pipeline implementation as part of my practical projects.

While I haven't yet had the opportunity to manage these technologies in a live production environment professionally, I understand the architecture and deployment workflows and can demonstrate my practical implementation.

I am confident that my 10 years of software development experience, combined with my cloud and DevOps knowledge, will help me contribute effectively to a cloud-native development team.

This answer is honest, professional, and confident.

