## 7. How to build confidence in interviews

I want you to follow these five rules:

1. Don't compare yourself with someone who has 10 years of production AWS experience. Your software engineering experience is valuable.
2. Practice explaining your architecture without looking at notes.
3. Every day, spend 30 minutes answering technical interview questions aloud.
4. Practice troubleshooting, not just theory. Interviewers often ask what happens when a deployment fails or a pod crashes.
5. Don't memorize answers. Understand the reason behind every technical decision.

One important thing: You don't need to know everything before applying. Start applying while continuing to improve your skills.

