# 9\. My final career advice

There are three things I want you to remember:

1. Your 10 years of .NET experience should remain at the center of your profile.
2. Your AWS, Kubernetes, and CI/CD practical skills should differentiate you from other .NET candidates.
3. Don't wait until you complete all 45 days to apply. Start applying in the first week while preparing.

One additional recommendation: Be ready to discuss one project deeply. Interviewers are often more impressed by someone who can explain one complete architecture, its trade-offs, failures, and troubleshooting than someone who simply knows 20 AWS services.

Your target is not to convince interviewers that you know everything. Your target is to demonstrate that you can design, develop, deploy, and troubleshoot a modern .NET application.

